    {
      "key": "animation.layersIn",
      "section": "panels",
      "label": "Open",
      "description": "How long shell panels take to appear, and with which curve.",
      "help": "Each panel keeps its own entrance: the sidebars slide in from their side, the bar slides in, the dock, the shortcut guide (Super+F1) and the on-screen keyboard (Super+K) rise from the bottom, and the wallpaper selector drops from the top. The volume and brightness indicator, the media controls, the bar tooltips, the authenticator (Super+O), the AI quota panel and the display controls (Super+P) pop in. Notification popups only fade in, with a curve of their own and a much shorter time than the one shown here; the overview (Super), the session menu, the region selector, the widget layer (Super+G) and the system password dialog (polkit) do not use this animation.",
      "keywords": [
        "layers",
        "capas",
        "panel",
        "paneles",
        "sidebar",
        "barra lateral",
        "dock",
        "open panel",
        "abrir panel",
