      "key": "animation.layersOut",
      "section": "panels",
      "label": "Close",
      "description": "How long shell panels take to go away, and with which curve.",
      "help": "Each panel leaves the way it came in: the sidebars slide back to their side, the bar slides out, the dock, the shortcut guide (Super+F1) and the on-screen keyboard (Super+K) sink to the bottom, and the wallpaper selector rises to the top. The volume and brightness indicator, the media controls, the bar tooltips, the authenticator (Super+O), the AI quota panel and the display controls (Super+P) shrink away. Notification popups only fade out, with a curve of their own that this card does not change; the overview (Super), the session menu, the region selector, the widget layer (Super+G) and the system password dialog (polkit) do not use this animation.",
